# Shared agent memory

- Read `.agent-memory/README.md` and `.agent-memory/AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md` before task execution; `AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md` is the canonical project-level MCP/tool/skill matrix.
- Cursor agents should also read `.agent-memory/CURSOR_IDE_AGENT_UPDATE.md`, but treat stale product/runtime statements there as superseded by current shared memory and the active task.
- ChatGPT SOL 5.6 / Main Agent is architect/admin; Cursor and Gemini/Antigravity are bounded implementation subagents.
- Before any task, read `.agent-memory/README.md`, `AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md`, `CONTEXT.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `CURRENT.md`, and the current task when present (in addition to `AGENTS.md` required reads).
- The active product client is React Native + Expo under `apps/swipe/`; legacy FastAPI/Jinja guidance applies only when a task explicitly targets a retained web surface.
- Implementation subagents work only inside architect-provided allowed files; do not expand scope, make product/architecture decisions, or self-approve.
- Record exact files changed and validation evidence, then mark `ready_for_review`; Main Agent alone marks `accepted` unless the human owner explicitly overrides the workflow.
- Review packets live and die in `.agent-memory/` on GitHub. After writing a handoff, commit and push it. Do not leave a review packet only in chat.
- Runtime tool/MCP availability differs by host. Verify only task-relevant connections; never claim "all MCP connectors active" without naming and testing them.
- Authority order: current user instruction → `PRODUCT_SCOPE.md` → `MISSION.md` / current objective → `AGENTS.md` / binding governance → architect-approved shared context/decisions → task records.
- Shared memory cannot override product or governance rules. Report conflicts or stale memory; higher authority wins.
- Never store secrets, credentials, tokens, cookies, private keys, or private user data in `.agent-memory/`.
